{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he said: Send me, for the dawn has risen.</b> For I can no longer bring you to the point of denying Eloah, after you have set your heart and mind on the rising of the dawn, as explained. 'And he said: I will not send you unless you bless me' (Genesis 32:27) — that you should acknowledge to me that you cannot prevail against me in the matter of seeing and contemplating the existence of El, blessed be He, so that the evil angel will answer Amen against his will, and the prosecutor will become the defender, as Samael does on Yom Kippur."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The opening word carries a superfluent dagesh/patach marker in the source; normalized to standard וַיֹּאמֶר without comment. The adverbial כָּאָמוּר ('as explained') appears to refer to a preceding comment on the same verse not included here."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:41.167672686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}